# UP6b, correction I1: a device resumes and then leaves for good. Inside the 30 s window the sweep's
# re-proposal is a no-op; after it, the re-proposal re-arms the row and appends a kind-0 row, the
# members queue it again, the Remove is committed and the leaf is gone.
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
group call kind=call target=ebebebebebebebebebebebebebebebeb community=none creator=alice
join bob call via=external
sync alice
absent bob call
sync alice
resume bob call withdrawn=1
sync alice
absent bob call
sync alice
send alice call the late flush was a no-op
expect_decrypts bob call the late flush was a no-op
advance_clock 31s
absent bob call
expect_425 send alice call the re-armed Remove stands
sync alice
commit alice call
expect_reject E_LEAF_NOT_CURRENT send bob call am I still in the call
expect_reject E_LEAF_NOT_CURRENT resume bob call
